[E-NOT-A-RECORD] Error: braces after `Circle` are its first argument, a `Text`, not its fields
   ╭─[ reject/ctor-braces-bracket-declared-fields.sw:8:24 ]
   │
 8 │ def c: Shape := Circle { id = "a", radius = 1 }
   │                        ────────────┬───────────  
   │                                    ╰───────────── this record is not a field's value
   │ 
   │ Note: `Circle` is declared with its fields in brackets, so braces after it are its first argument, not its fields; to give fields by name, write `Circle (id := …) (radius := …)`, or declare it `| Circle { … }`
───╯
